   Loire Metropole Urban Community},
Abstract = {Wearable devices have made it possible for health providers to monitor a
   patient's health remotely using actuators, sensors and other mobile
   communication devices. Internet of Things for Medical Devices is poised
   to revolutionize the functioning of the healthcare industry by providing
   an environment where the patient data is transmitted via a gateway onto
   a secure cloud based platforms for storage, aggregation and analytics.
   This paper proposes new set of wearable devices- a smart neck band,
   smart wrist band and a pair of smart socks- to continuously monitor the
   condition of diabetic patients. These devices consist of different
   sensors working in tandem form a network that reports food intake, heart
   rate, skin moisture, ambient temperature, walking patterns and weight
   gain/loss. The devices with the aid of controllers send all the sensor
   values as a packet via Bluetooth to the Mobile App. With the help of
   Machine Learning algorithm, we have predicted the change in patient
   status and alert them.},
