   Construct (CSCEC); Sino Grp; Vantage Int (Holdings) Ltd; ASCE Hong Kong
   Sect; ASHRAE Hong Kong Chapter; CIBSE; Construct Ind Council (CIC);
   Chartered Inst Bldg (CIOB); Council Sustainable Dev; Emerald; Hong Kong
   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc},
Abstract = {Free spanning submarine pipelines are complicated systems with
   soil-pipe-fluid interaction under deadweight, internal fluid, external
   environment and dynamic load. The dynamic responses of free spanning
   submarine pipeline are affected by a lot of factors. The dynamic
   response in earthquake was studied by using an underwater shaking table.
   Experiments on many groups of different combinations of factors
   including seismic wave direction, transmitting materials, distance from
   seabed, water depth and the kind of wave were carried out. The results
   show that the dynamic response under horizontal seismic input is larger
   than that under vertical seismic input at the same amplitude; under sine
   wave the dynamic response of pipeline of mid span declines as the
   sediment concentration increases, but become stable when the pipeline is
   in deep water and longer distance from seabed.},
