Title = {Fate of Selected Heavy Metals in a Biological Wastewater Treatment
   System},
Booktitle = {RECENT ADVANCES IN ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE FROM THE EURO-MEDITERRANEAN AND
   SURROUNDING REGIONS, 2ND EDITION, EMCEI-2},
Series = {Environmental Science and Engineering-Environmental Engineering},
Year = {2021},
Pages = {157-163},
Note = {2nd Euro-Mediterranean Conference for Environmental Integration-EMCEI,
   Sousse, TUNISIA, OCT 10-13, 2019},
Abstract = {Carried out by human activity, micropollutants are one of the major
   environmental concerns. Among these micropollutants, heavy metals occupy
   an important position. Indeed, many micropollutants from human activity,
   particularly in urban areas, are eliminated in the water masses,
   degrading their quality and disrupting their good ecological
   functioning. Their presence in wastewater is one of the main causes of
   water and soil pollution. The purpose of this study was to evaluate
   heavy metals content in wastewater at the wastewater treatment plant of
   AL-HOCEIMA city, located on the Mediterranean coast in the north of
   Morocco. To this end, two composite samples, 24 h to be representative,
   were taken (raw water and treated water). Water volumes were collected
   using refrigerated (4 degrees C) autosamplers equipped with Teflon
   bottle hoses to prevent contamination. The content of heavy metals such
   as Cu, Zn, Fe, Mn, Cd, Pb, As, Ni, Ba, Cr, Co and Hg in wastewater was
   determined by Inductively Coupled Plasma Spectrometry (ICP-OES). The
   results showed that the content of heavy metals (Cu, Zn, Fe, Mn, Cd, Pb,
   As, Ni, Ba, Cr, Co and Hg) at the inlet of the treatment plant is
   relatively low, because of the low industrial activity in the region.
   This clearly confirms the domestic nature of the city wastewater. The
   removal efficiency of heavy metals was directly proportional to their
   initial values in raw wastewater. The reduction of heavy metals was as
   follows: Cd < Cu < Fe < Mn < Cu < Pb < Ni < Co < Ba < Zn < Cr < Hg.},
