   Technol HOME Program; Malardalen Univ, Future Energy Profile},
Abstract = {The blossom of economic growth accompanied with the rapid urbanization
   always associates with large amount of carbon emissions. The influences
   of economic structure on carbon emissions still need further
   investigation. The information-based network analysis can investigate
   the systematic robustness covering facets of both efficiency and
   redundancy from network structure perspective. This study adopts this
   method to detect the correlation between the robustness of embodied
   carbon network with carbon emission intensity, choosing China as a case
   study. The results show that the system robustness tends to show a
   negative correlation with carbon intensity, i.e. higher robustness, less
   carbon intensity. (C) 2016 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
