Abstract = {This paper draws on our work as an ESP teacher with the 2nd year
   students from The Faculty of Economics and Business Administration at
   Alexandru loan Cuza University of Iasi, Romania and its branch in Balti,
   The Republic of Moldova. Since one of the topics discussed during the
   English seminars is corporate social responsibility, we will present our
   students' perception of the matter based on the activities and exercises
   that were chosen to develop their active/ productive (speaking and
   writing) and passive/receptive (reading and listening) skills. Thus, we
   will account for their views on the topic and assess them taking into
   account the students' two different backgrounds, the Romanian and
   Moldavian one. Finally, we will outline the results to several
   Likert-scale statements on CSR that our students were asked to provide
   and interpret them.},
