   Management (12BM), MALAYSIA, APR 18-20, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {This paper explored the performance dimension of religion based
   co-operatives in Malaysia, as a study of this nature had not been
   attempted since nearly thirty years ago. Questionnaires were distributed
   using the purposive sampling method to obtain the perception of
   respondents from mosque co-operatives. Feedback from 116 respondents was
   analysed using exploratory factor analysis. A total of four factors
   namely; financial performance, growth and contribution, socioeconomic
   performance, and satisfaction and governance, were extracted using the
   principal component method with a varimax rotation. Group means scores
   were 4.99, 5.08, 5.12 and 5.26 respectively while the Cronbach's Alpha
   were 0.973, 0.950, 0.938 and 0.829 respectively. Based on the mean group
   score, the major performance dimension for mosque co-operatives was
   satisfaction and governance, followed by socioeconomic performance,
   growth and contribution, and financial performance.},
