Note = {Conference on ENTERprise Information Systems (CENTERIS) / International
   Conference on Project MANagement (ProjMAN) / International Conference on
   Health and Social Care Information Systems and Technologies (HCIST),
   Troia, PORTUGAL, OCT 15-17, 2014},
Abstract = {Projects are complex works subjected to significant time, budget and
   quality constraints. One or the greatest challenges in project
   management still remaining unsolved is determining what is necessary to
   do in order to achieve success or failure. According to the specialized
   literature, both concepts of success factors and failure causes in
   projects are largely subjective and therefore difficult to quantify,
   depending on the point of view of the stakeholders involved. This paper
   tries to determine the most frequent failure causes and the most
   important success factors for ICT projects carried out in Spain within
   the framework of a much wider research, by means of a worldwide
   empirical survey carried out among project managers intended to gather
   their personal perceptions. The survey is based on a questionnaire
   anonymously distributed through a professional internet network. (C)
   2014 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
