Note = {International Workshop on Intelligent Information Technology (2WINTECH),
   Cheonan, SOUTH KOREA, OCT 20-22, 2016},
Abstract = {Ecohydrology (EH) is a sub-discipline of hydrology that focuses on
   ecological processes occurring within the hydrological cycle by using
   such processes for enhancing environmental sustainability. The three
   principles of ecohydrology are hydrological, ecological and ecological
   engineering. Groundwater resources conservation in Batu City East Java
   needs to be a priority attention because the location is in the upper
   water catchment area of Brantas. The paper will show the application of
   ecohydrology for groundwater resources conservation by relating the
   vegetation cover to evapotranspiration process and the impact of
   vegetation types to groundwater recharge in the study area. The Land Use
   and Land Cover Change during 2003-2015 bring such impact to groundwater
   recharge will be observed. The depletion of forest area is 562.68 Ha or
   3\%, it also happens on agriculture land and grassland. The urban area
   has to increase significantly as an impact of tourism policy. Land use
   and land cover change also increase total runoff 11\% and decrease
   evapotranspiration 15\%. The hydrological parameter such as rainfall,
   wind velocity, humidity, and sun radiation are very potential for
   groundwater conservation. But ecological parameter such as vegetation as
   a land cover has changed. The application of ecohydrology can give a
   contribution to environmental sustainability in groundwater
   conservation.},
