Note = {International Conference on Global Health and the United Arab Emirates -
   Asia-Middle East Connections, United Arab Emirates Univ, Al Ain, U ARAB
   EMIRATES, JAN 04-08, 2010},
Abstract = {As per the World Health Organization's global noncommunicable disease
   (NCD) strategy, data on health perceptions and behaviours are critical
   to designing and tailoring interventions to slow rising NCD prevalence
   and the toll on public health and economic well-being. Intervention
   planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation require
   understanding the relevant public's sense of personal risk, prevention
   awareness, and willingness to undertake preventative measures, as well
   as structural barriers impeding engagement in healthy behaviours,
   seeking treatment, and managing illness. This article details the design
   features and challenges of a study focused on the aforementioned
   features in Chennai, India. These features and challenges have relevance
   across Asia. As such, communication and collaboration between Asian
   researchers and program planners can enrich results for all involved.
   Establishing such a forum should be high on Asia's global health agenda.},
