Number = {1-4},
Pages = {123-130},
Note = {11th World Congress of the
   World-Association-for-Dynamic-Psychiatry/XXIVth International Symposium
   of the German-Academy-for-Psychoanalysis, FACHHOCHSCHULE MUNCHEN-PASING,
   MUNICH, GERMANY, MAR 04-08, 1997},
Organization = {World Assoc Dynam Psychiat; German Acad Psychoanal},
Abstract = {The author examines from various standpoints the topic of abolishing the
   splitting between biological and psychological phenomena in psychiatry:
   Freud's hope and question that in future psychological phenomena might
   prove to be definitely biophysiological, led him to the new infant
   research findings and their insights into the development of perception
   as well as to the physiological findings of brain research including the
   techniques of PET and SPECT. The concept of `'representation'' to him
   becomes a model for explaining the changes in the patient's personality
   effected by the therapeutic relationship between physician and patient.
   This concept means: perceiving and experiencing the environment and
   other persons can be realized ana responded to from birth on in
   different ways. In addition the author refers to new research work
   showing that psychotherapy leads to the same physiological changes as
   psychopharmacological treatments.},
