Note = {1st World Conference on Psychology and Sociology (PSYSOC), Antalya,
   TURKEY, NOV 27-DEC 01, 2012},
Organization = {Acad World Educ \& Res Ctr},
Abstract = {Development of posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) in parents of
   premature neonates has been recently described. Several source of stress
   have been hypothesized, however causes of PTDS and emotional reaction of
   the parents of premature birth hospitalized in a neonatal intensive care
   unit (NICU) remain largely undefined. We demonstrated that alteration of
   parental role and a history of anxiety have a crucial role in the
   development of PTSD in the parents of premature neonates.
   Familiarization with neonatal intensive care unit environment and
   increasing participation of the parents in the care of neonates during
   the first weeks of life improves parental role perception. Early
   involvement of the parents and especially of the mothers in the neonatal
   care, in particular if the risk of anxiety is consistent, should be
   considered a primary objective to prevent a PTSD. (C) 2013 The Authors.
   Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
