Pages = {88-92},
Note = {2nd International Multi-Conference on Society, Cybernetics and
   Informatics, Orlando, FL, JUN 29-JUL 02, 2008},
Organization = {Int Inst Informat \& System},
Abstract = {This article aims to bring a better understanding of the effectiveness
   of virtual learning communities (VLC) in a science teaching course. This
   course is part of a Teacher education program at the University of
   Ottawa, taught in the French sector of the Faculty of Education. Two
   groups of teacher candidates who participated to the virtual learning
   community were included in the study. The answers and comments provided
   in an assignment about their perceptions of the VLC were analysed.
   Results show that the VLC give future teachers an in-depth understanding
   of the theoretical perspectives brought by the articles that an
   individual reading may not have provided. The VLC give the students
   three overarching benefits, namely cognitive, social and ideological.
   These benefits coincide with the dimensions of the learning community
   described as a social construct by Schussler (2003).},
