Organization = {Portuguese Soc Occupat Safety \& Hygiene; Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ
   Porto, Fac Engn; Univ Lisbon, Fac Human Kinet; Polytechn Univ Catalonia;
   Tech Univ Delft; Faculdade Motricidade Humana; DELTA; EXIM; ACT;
   European Agcy Safety \& Hlth Work; Lavoro},
Abstract = {The noise affects negatively the quality of life of a big part of the
   worldwide population. Besides that, the health and cognitive effects can
   become preponderant, due to the big amount of people exposed to the
   environmental noise and the chronic character of that exposure. This
   study intended to evaluate the personal and diary exposition to the
   noises the students, using a Dosimeter. The subjects of the sample
   carried this instrument, to a maximum of six hours, as well as a road
   book, in which they wrote down the locals where they've been, the
   activities they did and the time they did it, and even, completed a
   questionnaire on the perception of noise levels and their influence on
   health. It was verified that the students are exposed to higher levels
   of noises than the recommended by the WHO leading to discomfort.},
