Abstract = {Quality parent-child relationship is often associated with children's
   behaviour. Its style of upbringing, family environment, education,
   morals and discipline are an important factor in building a healthy
   adolescent personality and prosperous. This means they are healthy
   mentally, physically and psychology. Level of parental involvement with
   the activities carried out in schools also help improve the emotional
   wellbeing of children in order to build successful children understand
   the world as a teenager, is related to emotional health and well-being
   of young people. Parental involvement, either positive or negative gives
   impact on self-esteem and social skills of adolescents. Parental styles
   have a significant impact on children's development. This article review
   research related to adolescents' perceptions of parental involvement,
   the parenting style related to emotional well-being of adolescents,
