   2019)},
Series = {IOP Conference Series-Earth and Environmental Science},
Year = {2019},
Volume = {344},
Note = {5th International Conference on Water Resource and Environment (WRE) /
   1st International Conference on Advances in Civil and Ecological
   Engineering Research (ACEER), Macau Univ Sci \& Technol, Macao, PEOPLES
   R CHINA, JUN 16-19, 2019},
Abstract = {Estimating farmland shelterbelt water use is important for oasis water
   resource management and agricultural development. Meteorological
   measurements combined with sap flow techniques were applied to study the
   mechanism of water consumption in farmland shelterbelt. Results showed
   that mean daily sap flow velocity and canopy transpiration of farmland
   shelterbelt varied from 429 +/- 247 kg m(-2) d(-1) to 1495 +/- 634 kg
   m(-2) d(-1) and from 0.45 mm d(-1) to 1.58 mm d(-1). A multinomial model
   account for 81.3\% of the variation was applied to explain canopy
   transpiration. Cross validation showed it provided good predictions of
   canopy transpiration for farmland shelterbelt. Knowing the relationship
   between climate variability and farmland shelterbelt water consumption
   is benefit for the management of water resources in oasis agriculture.},
