Abstract = {In order to improve the flocculating activity of the bioflocculant
   produced by B3 (named MBFB3), the optimum flocculating characteristics
   were determined by a serious of experiments. Many factors in Kaolin
   suspension, such as the concentration of bioflocculant, metal ions,
   temperature and pH could influence the flocculating activity After the
   orthogonal analysis of the influencing factors in flocculation system,
   the most optimum condition for flocculating were adding 0.4g kaolin in
   color comparison tube of 100ml, 1\% CaCl2 lml, bioflocculant lml, pH
   about 5.0, standing 5min after quickly shaking 10 times and slowly 10
   times after 10 times, sampling at the point of 75ml, absorbance
   measurement.under 660nm.},
