Pages = {343-350},
Note = {International Multidisciplinary Scientific Conferences on Social
   Sciences and Arts (SGEM 2014), Albena, BULGARIA, SEP 01-10, 2014},
Organization = {Bulgarian Acad Sci; Acad Sci Czech Republ; Latvian Acad Sci; Polish Acad
   Sci; Russian Acad Sci; Serbian Acad Sci \& Arts; Slovak Acad Sci Intro;
   Natl Acad Sci Ukraine; Natl Acad Sci Armenia; Sci Counc Japan; World
   Acad Sci TWAS; European Acad Sci, Arts \& Lett; Acad Fine Arts Zagreb
   Croatia; Croatian Acad Sci \& Arts; Acad Sci Moldova; Montenegrin Acad
   Sci \& Arts; Georgian Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {The difficulties in life connected with upbringing of a child with
   special needs lead to high level of distress for parents. Mainly
   negative influence of the child's disease upon intrafamilial and
   extrafamilial functioning, psychological well-being of parents define
   the necessity of regular help for such people. Aims of rational-emotive
   behavior therapy (REBT) correspond to psychological problems of
   relatives of children with special needs. As few sources show, REBT has
   a significant potential in assisting parents with taking under control
   negative emotions. This increases parents' effectiveness in taking care,
   upbringing and reaching maximal possible level of development of a
   special child. The present report describes an application of REBT to a
   mother of a child with special needs. Methods: We report the case of a
   29-year-old mother of a 5-year-old boy with cerebral palsy and
   intellectual disability. The woman showed partial denial of the child's
   grave condition, evident fears for his life, outbursts of anger directed
   at people around her and the boy, on the background of a lack of
   awareness of feeling of guilt. A usage of cognitive, emotional and
   behavioral techniques of REBT is described. A range of irrational
   beliefs underlying her psychological problems is presented. Results: The
   positive changes in acceptance of the child's condition and coping with
   frustrations have been achieved. Conclusions: A conclusion about
   effectiveness of the studying approach of helping parents of children
   with special needs and about necessity of further research in this field
   is made.},
